Stop [E3001]: `panic: the card was declined`
  --> transact_panic_rollback.jet:37 in withdraw
     |
37 |         panic("the card was declined")
     |         ^^^^^
 Why: The program hit a `panic`, `assert`, or `assert_eq` call that failed, a bounds/key check triggered at runtime, or another program-side stop. The shared report boundary owns the program-side stop; an unhandled entry error is a returned report, not E3001. Jet file and line are shown in Jet terms (I2).
 Fix: Fix the logic that led to the failure. Program-side stops exit 70 through the shared boundary; unhandled entry errors print their report and exit 1; exit 101 is reserved for Jet defects.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3001
